    If $f^{-1}_{i \to j}(\sigma) = \varnothing$ we set $\DP_H[k,\sigma] = 0$.
    Notice that computing $f^{-1}_{i \to j}(\sigma)$ requires $n^{\bO(2^\cw)}$ time,
    thus by \cref{eq:cw:relabel} we can fill the table $\DP_H[\cdot,\cdot]$ in time $n^{\bO(2^\cw)}$.


    \begin{claim}\label{claim:cw:relabel}
        Let $H = \rho_{i \to j}(H')$.
        Assume that for $k \in [0,n]$ and $\sigma \in \Sigma$,
        $\DP_{H'}[k,\sigma]$ is equal to the number of subsets of
